      "note": "Ports the three DIE overlay alternatives and ten independently detecting early-NSIS entry-point patterns. Native PE origins use a conservative declared CLR-directory presence guard; DIE PE.isNet additionally validates CLI metadata. The overlay resolver also permits the native reader's raw modern header carrier. Redirected %% is exactly one ANSI byte (0x20-0x7f), enforced by masked atoms. The DIE manifest-only detection branch is intentionally outside this bounded signature path; version strings, compression-method hints and solid metadata are not returned by fast_detect. Detection is a family candidate only: reader opening and size/carving still validate structure, CRC and supported payloads. DIE overlay location differs from the native reader's arbitrary 512-byte aligned MZ search; arbitrary aligned embedded headers outside the resolved overlay are not searched here.",
